# Git branches (Fluxa)

Full spec: [docs/fluxa/development-spec.md](../../docs/fluxa/development-spec.md) §4. Summary at repo root: [development-spec.md](../../development-spec.md).

## Long-lived branches

| Branch | Role |
|--------|------|
| `dev` | Integration: merge all `feature/*`, `fix/*`, `refactor/*` here first |
| `main` | Release line: merge from `dev` when stable; not for day-to-day Fluxa features |

## Required flow

```text
feature/* | fix/* | refactor/*  →  dev  →  main
```

- Branch **from `dev`**, not from `main`.
- **Do not** commit new Fluxa product work directly on `main`.
- Upstream FlClash: **`sync/flclash-<version>`** only — merge upstream there, then into **`dev`**, then **`dev` → `main`** after checks. Never large `upstream/main` merge on `main` or `dev` directly.

## Before starting work

```bash
git checkout dev && git pull origin dev
git checkout -b feature/<short-name>
```

## Remote on GitHub (`origin`)

**Only these branches may exist on `origin`:**

- `main`
- `dev`

`feature/*`, `fix/*`, `refactor/*`, `sync/*`, and `release/*` are **local-only** (or short-lived on your machine). **Do not** `git push origin feature/...` or push other topic branches to GitHub.

After merging locally into `dev`:

```bash
git checkout dev
git merge feature/<short-name>
git push origin dev
# optional release: merge dev → main, then git push origin main
```

Delete stale remote topic branches if they were pushed by mistake:

```bash
git push origin --delete feature/<name>
```
